{"id": "lg_elec-2026-10-23-006", "date": "2026-10-23", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 43, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_elec", "lg_display"], "customers": ["lg_elec"], "suppliers": ["lg_display"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["record", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 1.0, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "涉及財報", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "LG Display returns to profit in Q3 2026 as OLED reaches a record 67% of revenue, raises its large OLED shipment outlook and plans to restart idle lines", "content": "<p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/lg-oled\">LG Display</a> reported its financial results for the third quarter of 2026, with revenue of $4.71 billion, up 12% from the previous quarter but down 10% from Q3 2025. The company swung to an operating profit of $188 million, compared to an operating loss of $81 million in Q2 2026, although profit was down 42% from a year earlier. Earnings (EBIDTA) reached $911 million (a 19% margin), and net income was $567 million (compared to a net loss of $314 m", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/lg-display-returns-profit-q3-2026-oled-reaches-record-67-revenue-raises-its", "type": "rss"}]}
